{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q1870264","formula":"CaCe₂(CO₃)₃F₂","hill":"C3CaCe2F2O9","elements":["C","O","F","Ca","Ce"],"composition":{"C":3.0,"F":2.0,"O":9.0,"Ca":1.0,"Ce":2.0},"names":{"en":"Parisite-(Ce)","uk":"Паризит-(Ce)"},"descriptions":{"en":"Parisite is a rare mineral consisting of cerium, lanthanum and calcium fluoro-carbonate, Ca(Ce,La)2(CO3)3F2. Parisite is mostly parisite-(Ce), but when neodymium is present in the structure the mineral becomes parisite-(Nd). It is found only as crystals, which belong to the trigonal or monoclinic pseudo-hexagonal system and usually have the form of acute double pyramids terminated by the basal planes; the faces of the hexagonal pyramids are striated horizontally, and parallel to the basal plane there is a perfect cleavage.","uk":"Паризит-(Ce) - мінерал групи паризиту, фтор-карбонат кальцію та церію. Хімічна формула: 1. За Є. Лазаренком: CaCe2F2[CO3]3."},"fame":9,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1870264","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parisite-%28Ce%29","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9F%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%B7%D0%B8%D1%82-%28Ce%29","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"photo","name":"Wikimedia Commons","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Parisite-(Ce)-180017.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q948415","formula":"CaCe(CO₃)₂F","names":{"en":"Synchysite-(Ce)"},"elements":["C","O","F","Ca","Ce"],"fame":9,"kind":"crystal"},{"id":"Q3787372","formula":"BaCe(CO₃)₂F","names":{"en":"Huanghoite-(Ce)","uk":"Хуанхіт"},"elements":["C","O","F","Ba","Ce"],"fame":